The rule for k_recovery says: 'The object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT.' The cell fence[ S A ] contains a fence with two parts: S and A. The rewritten text fence[ S A ] B adds one part after the fence. The recovered object is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one. In the original, the last object inside the fence is A. In the rewritten, the last object inside the fence is B. Since A and B are different objects, the recovered object changes, so the answer moves.